s there  today and turn it into non-stop  campaigning against what i think is a  pretty hopeless government i think labor  does have a chance but be realistic  there's no point going around saying we  are going to win you've got to say we  want to win we can win but here's all  the things we have to do yeah what  should be the focus now you talk about  campaigning and really as you mentioned  with covid a lot of people saying where  is shakir stamina our new labour leader  in his defense you know it was locked  down it was coving he wasn't as visible  as he would have been  under normal circumstances so where do  you want to see him he can't focus on  everything what should he focus on  in the next few months  well i think he  he actually answered that in the speech  i thought he when he talked about  you can you good society you can't have  the good society without the strong  economy you can't have a strong economy  without the good society now that is  that's what i call a framing message  so what does the good society mean what  does the strong economy mean how do we  get that i thought he spoke very well  about how co would expose weaknesses  that have been there for too long i was  pleased that he linked even though  johnson's terrible he actually said this  is about a decade of conservative role  so focus on the weaknesses that have  been exposed and how you as leader of  the labour party of the labour party are  going to address those and actually you  say you can't do everything  it's true you can't do everything all of  the time but you can be engaged every  single day on one of the big challenges  that he set out there today and i think  it's important that now that he becomes  much more visible than he's been that  the shadow cabinet becomes much more  visible that the front bench becomes  much more visible because frankly you  know in the last year or so and caveat  of course if the government's if there's  a national crisis the government is  going to 